        <a:p><a:r><a:t>Root cause is likely accumulated friction rather than one incident [needs-verification — driver not isolatable from current data]. Churn figures (5/11/8 FY23/24/25) appear in the narrative without a cited source — treat as author-stated. Small sample (28 respondents) but directional signal is real. Follow up all 16 detractors within 30 days before drawing conclusions. Note: industry_benchmarks.csv contains a 2025 NPS figure of +52, but the quarterly nps_survey_results.csv shows all 2025 quarters negative — these appear to use different methodologies; the comparison was removed from the slide face.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>── Supporting claims ──</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>• "Recurring themes: team chemistry, turnaround time, value for money, communication"</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>  — ./Data/clients/nps_survey_results.csv</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>• "Repeat-client revenue 68% vs. 60% industry average"</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>  — ./Data/market/industry_benchmarks.csv</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t></a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>── Data sources ──</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:t>• nps_distribution (pie_chart): ./Data/clients/nps_survey_results.csv</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody>
